@essay rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · DORIAN · THE MACHINERY AROUND HIM"
# The machinery around him
drop: Dorian built most of the machinery the other dossiers describe. The Broadcast became sophisticated under him, and the Trials became its most valuable property (TL). It holds forty percent of the Covenant Score through narrative priority decisions nobody discloses (TR).
What presses on him is older. He sits on the throne by survivorship, the son of an heir removed in 2061 (FR 35, 39). The ledger in his keeping names Elias (FR 44). His heir is twenty-five, unmarried, and keeps a room on the Administrative Side his father doesn't know about (CR). His elder son is officially dead, and the paperwork was quiet (TL).
INTERPRETATION: A man who governs by being loved has to keep the people closest to him from looking at the paper.
